BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:World on a Plate Guest Lecture Series: Spiro Stefanou — Washingt
 on\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261027T161000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261027T170000
DTSTAMP:20261019T222410Z
UID:e30bd94599da84aef267e8913c67@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures & Speakers\,Washington\, DC\,United St
 ates
DESCRIPTION:World on A Plate \, a class designed by world-renowned chef an
 d humanitarian José Andrés\, is an exploration of the many ways in whic
 h food and society interact. In this course and expanded guest lecture ser
 ies\, we invite you to think deeply about food in its many different roles
  – as a critical factor in public health\, as an industry\, as a science
 \, as the medium of the craft of cooking\, and as a political instrument. 
 Join Spiro Stefanou \, former administrator of the USDA Economic Research 
 Service\, for this lecture. RSVP here.\nCategory: Lectures & Speakers\nOr
 iginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/world-on-a-plate-guest-lect
 ure-series-spiro-stefanou
LOCATION:Phillips Hall (Academic Center)\, 801 22nd Street NW
